Live draw: a texture smaller than the colour surface it aliases reads the surface's top-left samples, texel for
sample (not the whole surface scaled into it). Toro's own patch (7xxx).
What: when a fragment texture aliases a render surface at the same (location, offset) and is smaller than it,
the bind now gets a texture of exactly the declared w x h holding the top-left w x h of the surface (CopyTextureRegion
with a w x h source box, kept per surface and size, recopied only after a GPU write or guest re-upload into the
surface), so normalised coordinates, clamp, filtering and texel size see the texture the guest declared. Only when
the mapping is provably 1:1: a linear (LN) 2D texture whose pitch equals the surface's guest pitch and whose texel
size equals the surface's. Otherwise (and for exact-size aliases, and textures larger than the surface) the whole
surface is bound as before. Same technique as KZ3 patch 2063 for zeta reads (a 2D SRV cannot select a sub-rectangle).
Why: the title screen's scene pass sets SURFACE_FORMAT 0xA0B5148 (A8R8G8B8, antialias 5 = square-centred 4 samples),
raw clip 2560x1440, colour0 0x01FB0000, pitch 10240, viewport 1280x720. rsx_dsp_get_surface multiplies the clip by
the 2x2 sample grid (KZ3 patch 2016), so the host surface is 5120x2880 (`[rsx-target] ... off=0x01FB0000 fmt=0x8
pitch=10240 clip=0,0+5120x2880`); the game draws only its viewport, 2560x1440 samples, which is all the guest memory
holds (pitch 10240 = 2560 x 4 B; tile 7 is 0xE10000 = 10240 x 1440 B). The oversized clip is harmless on hardware.
The downsample then samples 0x01FB0000 as fmt 0xA5 (A8R8G8B8 LN) 2560x1440 (`[alias-hit] tex 0:0x01FB0000 fmt=0xA5
2560x1440 -> surface[1] 0:0x01FB0000 5120x2880`): bound to the whole surface, it took the scene from the top-left
quarter only, so every later pass (640x360 bloom chain, final composite) showed the scene in a corner of the frame.
On the RSX, texel (x,y) of a linear texture is the byte at y*pitch + x*bpp, which for equal pitch and texel size is
sample (x,y) of the surface.
Switch: LD_SWIN=0 = old behaviour (logged once as "[swin] on|off (LD_SWIN)").
Verify: build tlp.exe; run to the title screen with LD_ALIAS_DBG=1: "[swin] 0:0x1FB0000 surface 5120x2880
pitch=10240 -> window 2560x1440" once and "[alias-subrect] tex 0:0x01FB0000 fmt=0xA5 2560x1440 pitch=10240 ->
surface[N] 5120x2880 texels [0,2560)x[0,1440)"; no "[alias-subrect] keep whole surface" line for 0x01FB0000 (that
line means the texture pitch differed: the old binding was kept). The title-screen scene fills the frame instead of
its top-left quarter. Exact-size alias hits (1280x720, 640x360, 320x180) are unchanged.
ASSUMPTION: a write into a surface that bypasses ld_surface_note_write / ld_gv_upload_rows leaves the window stale.
Upstream candidate (general alias fix).

